hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"162","Inna lillahi ma akhadha wa lahu ma a'ta. Wa kullu shay'in 'indahu bi'ajal musamma... Falisbir waltahtasib. Wa in qala: 'A'zam Allahu ajraka, wa ahsana 'aza'aka wa ghaffira li-mayyitika' fahasanan.. Indeed, to Allah belongs what He has taken and to Him belongs what He has given. And everything with Him is for a specified term... So be patient and seek reward (from Allah). And if one says: 'May Allah magnify your reward, and improve your consolation, and forgive your deceased,' it is good."
"163","Bismillāh wa `alā sunnati Rasūlillāh. With the Name of Allah, and according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah. Reference: Abu Dawud 3/314 with an authentic chain. Ahmad also recorded it with the wording: With the Name of Allah, and according to the religion of the Messenger of Allah. Its chain is also authentic."
